Date: Sun, 15 Feb 2026 22:27:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/25] =?UTF-8?q?kn5000:=20Major=20driver=20rework=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20subcpu=20payload,=20control=20panel=20HLE,=20keybed?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Make the KN5000 driver functional from power-on through normal
operation:

- NVRAM factory defaults: Seed backup SRAM from program ROM so
  firmware passes validation and proceeds with subcpu payload
  transfer instead of entering diagnostic mode.

- SubCPU memory map: Map tone generator (0x100000), DSP (0x130000),
  inter-CPU latch (0x120000), and waveform RAM stubs to silence
  unmapped memory warnings and allow the firmware to communicate
  between main and sub CPUs.

- Inter-CPU latch: Logging wrappers and perfect_quantum() scheduling
  for reliable HDMA payload transfer of the 524KB sub CPU program.

- Control panel HLE (new files): Implements the serial protocol
  between main CPU and control panel MCU (whose ROM is not dumped).
  Handles button scanning with INTA-driven sessions, LED output
  routing to layout elements, and rotary encoder input.

- Keybed HLE: Injects note events at 0x110000/0x110002 for the
  subcpu's ToneGen_Read_Voice_Data routine. 61 keys (C2-C7),
  no default PC keyboard bindings to avoid conflicts with control
  panel button mappings (use MAME Tab menu to assign).

- MIDI ports: Properly wired MIDI in/out on serial port 0.

- Layout: LED output names updated for cpanel HLE compatibility.
